From 5f86e63d916985d310b94e97e061354a8181adbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 02:00:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(pathkernel): an Outside piece starts at the stock
 edge with a proved approach from the air

A stay-down link can now end with an approach from the air: a straight
stretch from the nearest place of the air to the start of an open piece
on a stock edge loop. The approach holds when it stays outside the
cutter-centre area, in the air or the edge band, clear of the part zone
and of each keep-out area by a tool radius, in the legal room, crosses
no cut, and the disc swept along it, less the swath of the next piece,
lies within a tool radius of the air (outside the stock). The way out to
the air uses the three tries of K4. The plan's transition table does not
change: the approach is a stretch of a proved stay link.

Measured again, no constant tuned: the disc band goes from 13/0/13 to
0/0/0 lifts and the dog-bone band from 15/0/15 to 0/0/0 (Auto, Inside,
Outside); the island pocket stays 7/7/5. The motion pin has 0 lifts and
0 crossing feeds on both fixtures. One approach on the dog bone arrives
at full width (follow-up #4272).

Refs #4254

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
